<title>DUBAI: Iran's Aghazadeh says D'Amato law no problem.</title>
<headline>Iran's Aghazadeh says D'Amato law no problem.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh was reported on Thursday as saying the U.S. Iran-Libya Sanctions Act was not affecting Iran's vital oil industry.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no problems because of the D'Amato law, and are receiving the usual cooperation with our trade and economic partners,&quot; Aghazadeh told the English-language Iran News.</p>
<p>The report was carried by the official IRNA news agency.</p>
<p>President Bill Clinton signed the Iran-Libya sanctions bill in August, which allows the president to punish non-U.S. firms which invest $40 million or more a year in Iran's oil and gas industries.</p>
</text>
